# Deleting a whole species, and deleting part of one.
#
# WHOLE SPECIES.  A rule that drops every molecule of a reactant pattern
# without the DeleteMolecules keyword (`A() -> 0`) deletes the species the
# pattern matched.  BioNetGen makes that SPECIES the rule's reaction center
# (RxnRule::find_reaction_center: "a Species delete rule will add Species as
# Rxn Center"), and matches with the same reaction center are one reaction
# (filter_identical_by_rxn_center).  So the rule fires ONCE per matching
# species, at k, however many of its molecules match the pattern and however
# the pattern names it.  NFsim attaches the delete to the pattern's first
# molecule -- "arbitrarily", in its own source -- and counts one instance per
# match of that molecule, and RuleMonkey did the same: 2k on an A.A dimer,
# and 2k or 1k on one A.B.A trimer depending on whether the rule was written
# A().B() or B().A().  NFsim's -cb and -bscb do not change it.
#
# Every whole-species pool below decays at k per species, so its count
# follows N*exp(-k*t):
#
#   Dim_any      `Ad() -> 0` on Ad.Ad                       was 2k
#   Dim_whole    `Aw(b!1).Aw(b!1) -> 0` on Aw.Aw            was 2k
#   Tri_A        `At() -> 0` on At.Bt.At                    was 2k
#   Tri_B        `Bb() -> 0` on Ab.Bb.Ab   (control)        1k
#   Tri_AB       `Aab().Bab() -> 0` on Aab.Bab.Aab          was 2k
#   Tri_BA       `Bba().Aba() -> 0` on Aba.Bba.Aba          1k
#   Mixed        `Am() -> 0` on Am monomers and Am.Am dimers, counted in
#                molecules: N*exp(-k*t) + 2N*exp(-k*t)      dimers were 2k
#   Assembled    `Ar() -> 0` while Ar monomers dimerize during the run, so
#                the per-complex count follows complexes as they form
#
# PART OF A SPECIES.  When the rule keeps some molecules of the pattern
# (`C(x!1).D(x!1) -> D(x)`), BNG2 deletes only the dropped ones, keyword or
# not, and without the keyword lets the reaction happen only if what is left
# forms exactly as many species as the rule has product patterns
# (RxnRule::apply_rule).  RuleMonkey read DeleteMolecules="0" as "delete the
# whole species" and took the kept molecules with it.  NFsim refuses such a
# rule outright, so this half has no NFsim reference at all.
#
#   Keep         `Ck(x!1).Dk(x!1) -> Dk(x)` on Ck.Dk: Ck decays at k, Dk stays N
#   Strand       the same rule on a C that also holds an E: deleting it would
#                leave two species for one product pattern, so it never fires
#   Bridge       `Xb(c!1).Cb(x!1,y!2).Yb(c!2) -> Xb(c) + Yb(c)` on Xb.Cb.Yb:
#                fires at k, Xb and Yb stay N
#   Ring         the same rule where Xb and Yb are also bonded directly: one
#                species is left for two product patterns, so it never fires
begin model
begin parameters
  N     2000
  k     1.0e-3
  kon   2.0e-6
end parameters
begin molecule types
  Ad(b)
  Aw(b)
  At(b)
  Bt(a,a)
  Ab(b)
  Bb(a,a)
  Aab(b)
  Bab(a,a)
  Aba(b)
  Bba(a,a)
  Am(b)
  Ar(b)
  Ck(x)
  Dk(x)
  Cs(x,y)
  Ds(x)
  Es(c)
  Xb(c,y)
  Cb(x,y)
  Yb(c,x)
  Xr(c,y)
  Cr(x,y)
  Yr(c,x)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  Ad(b!1).Ad(b!1)                          N
  Aw(b!1).Aw(b!1)                          N
  At(b!1).Bt(a!1,a!2).At(b!2)              N
  Ab(b!1).Bb(a!1,a!2).Ab(b!2)              N
  Aab(b!1).Bab(a!1,a!2).Aab(b!2)           N
  Aba(b!1).Bba(a!1,a!2).Aba(b!2)           N
  Am(b)                                    N
  Am(b!1).Am(b!1)                          N
  Ar(b)                                    N
  Ck(x!1).Dk(x!1)                          N
  Cs(x!1,y!2).Ds(x!1).Es(c!2)              N
  Xb(c!1,y).Cb(x!1,y!2).Yb(c!2,x)          N
  Xr(c!1,y!3).Cr(x!1,y!2).Yr(c!2,x!3)      N
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Dim_any    Ad()
  Molecules Dim_whole  Aw()
  Molecules Tri_A      Bt()
  Molecules Tri_B      Bb()
  Molecules Tri_AB     Bab()
  Molecules Tri_BA     Bba()
  Molecules Mixed      Am()
  Molecules Assembled  Ar()
  Molecules Keep_C     Ck()
  Molecules Keep_D     Dk()
  Molecules Strand_C   Cs()
  Molecules Bridge_C   Cb()
  Molecules Bridge_XY  Xb().Yb()
  Molecules Bridge_X   Xb()
  Molecules Ring_C     Cr()
end observables
begin reaction rules
  DimAny:    Ad() -> 0  k
  DimWhole:  Aw(b!1).Aw(b!1) -> 0  k
  TriA:      At() -> 0  k
  TriB:      Bb() -> 0  k
  TriAB:     Aab().Bab() -> 0  k
  TriBA:     Bba().Aba() -> 0  k
  Mixed:     Am() -> 0  k
  Dimerize:  Ar(b) + Ar(b) -> Ar(b!1).Ar(b!1)  kon
  Assembled: Ar() -> 0  k
  Keep:      Ck(x!1).Dk(x!1) -> Dk(x)  k
  Strand:    Cs(x!1).Ds(x!1) -> Ds(x)  k
  Bridge:    Xb(c!1).Cb(x!1,y!2).Yb(c!2) -> Xb(c) + Yb(c)  k
  Ring:      Xr(c!1).Cr(x!1,y!2).Yr(c!2) -> Xr(c) + Yr(c)  k
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
